Spirit Remote Control vendored browser assets

@xterm/xterm            5.5.0    xterm.js, xterm.css
@xterm/addon-fit        0.10.0   addon-fit.js
@xterm/addon-web-links  0.11.0   addon-web-links.js

Source: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/<package>@<version>/...
License: MIT for all three packages; the upstream LICENSE files are committed
alongside the fetched assets.

script/vendor_remote_control_assets downloads each file into this directory and
verifies it against the sha256 recorded in that script; LICENSE-xterm comes down
with them. Re-run it after changing a pin here. When the assets are absent the
browser client detects the missing window.Terminal global and shows
"Terminal viewer assets are not vendored in this build" instead of failing.

index.html loads xterm.js and addon-web-links.js as classic scripts before the
ES module entry point, because both ship UMD builds that define globals.
addon-fit.js is pinned and vendored but not loaded: the client sizes the
viewer with the D9 fit rule (fixed server cols/rows, font size chosen to fit)
rather than resizing the terminal to the container.
